---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="FAQ" description="Quick answers about the purpose, scope, and intent of Rethink Redaction.">
  <section class="section">
    <h1 class="h1">FAQ</h1>

    <div class="card" style="padding: 1.5rem;">
      <h2 class="h2">Is this legal advice?</h2>
      <p class="small">
        No. This site is public-interest guidance about readability and workflow design. Agencies should consult their counsel
        for jurisdiction-specific requirements.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <h2 class="h2">Are you asking agencies to reveal protected information?</h2>
      <p class="small">
        No. The goal is to protect sensitive fields while avoiding unnecessary full-page blackout that harms comprehension.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <h2 class="h2">What’s wrong with solid black boxes?</h2>
      <p class="small">
        They often erase headings, structure, and surrounding context. Even when compliant, they can create confusion,
        increase follow-up requests, and reduce public trust.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <h2 class="h2">What will Phase 1 include?</h2>
      <p class="small">
        Examples, printable checklists, and templates — designed to be simple for staff and clear for the public.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>